{% import '_partials/_card_chrome.html.twig' as chrome %}
{#
admin/insight_reports/_frame.html.twig — Admin → Reported mail.

Accepts:
  reports      — list<App\Domain\Monitoring\ReportedMail>, newest first, both kinds
  problems     — list<{problem, kind, count}>, biggest first, derived from `reports`
  pendingCount — how many of the whole table are unhandled, not how many of the list
  handledCount — how many are done, for the card that sweeps them away

ONE LIST, TWO KINDS. A mail an extractor should have understood and did not, and
a mail somebody found in the wrong tab. These were two panels with two export
buttons, which made sense to whoever wrote them and to nobody using them: the
question an admin brings to this page is "what is still mine to do", and that
question does not have two answers. The rows carry a badge saying which kind
they are, and everything else — triage, filters, selection, export — is the
same for both.

THE CHIPS ARE THE SELECTOR. Filtering is not decoration here: the export takes
what is ticked, and the way somebody ticks "the six about wrongly-sorted shop
mail" is to filter to that problem and press select-all. Which chips exist is
derived from the rows, because for a wrong tab the problem IS a pair of
categories and only this install knows which pairs it has produced.

Every row is a native <details>, exactly as the log browser's rows are. An admin
here is triaging — deciding which of forty mails is a shape worth acting on —
and forty mail bodies rendered flat is a page nobody scrolls to the bottom of.

No auto-refresh wraps this frame — see the note where it is embedded in
index.html.twig. The mutating forms post into this frame and get the re-rendered
list back, so nothing here navigates the page.
#}
{# Layout classes belong on the placeholder in admin/index.html.twig, not
   here: Turbo transplants this frame's CHILDREN into the frame already on
   the page and never copies its attributes, so a class written here reaches
   nothing. See tests/Infrastructure/Templating/TurboFrameClassesTest.php. #}
<turbo-frame id="admin-insight-reports">

    {% macro problem_label(problem) %}
        {%- if problem == 'no-insight' -%}
            {{ 'admin.insight_reports.problem.no_insight'|trans }}
        {%- else -%}
            {%- set pair = problem|split('>') -%}
            {{ ('tabs.' ~ pair[0])|trans }}<i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right text-[9px] text-ink-faint mx-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ ('tabs.' ~ pair[1])|trans }}
        {%- endif -%}
    {% endmacro %}
    {% import _self as report %}

    {# ── The pile ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="@container {{ chrome.shell() }}"
             data-controller="admin--report-selection ui--clipboard"
             {# `{n}` and not `%count%`: the number is substituted in the
                browser, but a literal `%count%` in the rendered page is
                indistinguishable from a translation that failed to interpolate
                — and there is a test asserting none reaches the HTML. #}
             data-admin--report-selection-count-label-value="{{ 'admin.insight_reports.selected'|trans({'%count%': '{n}'}) }}"
             data-admin--report-selection-filename-value="reported-mail.txt"
             data-ui--clipboard-confirm-text-value="{{ 'clipboard.copied'|trans }}"
             data-ui--clipboard-failed-text-value="{{ 'clipboard.copy_failed'|trans }}">

        {# The selected lines. ui--clipboard copies this; the download button
           saves it; the export form beside it posts the keys instead. #}
        <pre class="hidden"
             data-admin--report-selection-target="sink"
             data-ui--clipboard-target="source"></pre>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 {{ chrome.band() }}">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-flag text-xs text-zinc-400" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{{ 'admin.insight_reports.heading'|trans }}</h2>
            <span class="text-xs text-ink-faint">{{ 'admin.insight_reports.pending'|trans({ '%count%': pendingCount }) }}</span>

            {% if reports|length > 0 %}
                <div class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-1.5">
                    <span class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint tabular-nums mr-1"
                          data-admin--report-selection-target="count"></span>

                    <button type="button"
                            data-action="click->ui--clipboard#copy"
                            data-admin--report-selection-target="action"
                            title="{{ 'admin.insight_reports.copy_hint'|trans }}"
                            class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 h-8 px-3 rounded-pane border border-line
                                   text-[11px] text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover cursor-pointer transition-colors
                                   disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed">
                        <i data-ui--clipboard-target="icon" class="fa-solid fa-copy text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span data-ui--clipboard-target="label">{{ 'admin.insight_reports.copy'|trans }}</span>
                    </button>

                    <button type="button"
                            data-action="click->admin--report-selection#download"
                            data-admin--report-selection-target="action"
                            title="{{ 'admin.insight_reports.download_hint'|trans }}"
                            class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 h-8 px-3 rounded-pane border border-line
                                   text-[11px] text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover cursor-pointer transition-colors
                                   disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-download text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span>{{ 'admin.insight_reports.download'|trans }}</span>
                    </button>
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        {% if reports|length == 0 %}
            {# Calmly, and not as a table with no rows in it: nothing being
               reported is the ordinary state of a working install, not an
               empty result somebody should go looking for. #}
            <div class="{{ chrome.body() }}">
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">{{ 'admin.insight_reports.empty'|trans }}</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-ink-faint leading-relaxed">{{ 'admin.insight_reports.empty_hint'|trans }}</p>
            </div>
        {% else %}

            {# ── The chips ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
               Two groups, and they are not the same question. Status is about
               the work — is this one still mine — and problem is about the
               subject. An admin normally wants one of each: "the unhandled
               ones about mail landing in Promotions". #}
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-line">
                <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint mr-1">
                    {{ 'admin.insight_reports.filter'|trans }}
                </span>

                {% for status in ['pending', 'handled'] %}
                    <button type="button"
                            data-status="{{ status }}"
                            data-admin--report-selection-target="chip"
                            data-action="click->admin--report-selection#filter"
                            class="chip-filter">
                        {{ ('admin.insight_reports.filter_' ~ status)|trans }}
                    </button>
                {% endfor %}

                {% if problems|length > 1 %}
                    <span class="w-px h-4 bg-line mx-1" aria-hidden="true"></span>

                    {% for group in problems %}
                        <button type="button"
                                data-problem="{{ group.problem }}"
                                data-admin--report-selection-target="chip"
                                data-action="click->admin--report-selection#filter"
                                class="chip-filter">
                            {{ report.problem_label(group.problem) }}
                            <span class="text-ink-faint tabular-nums ml-1">{{ group.count }}</span>
                        </button>
                    {% endfor %}
                {% endif %}
            </div>

            <label class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 border-b border-line cursor-pointer
                          text-[11px] text-ink-faint hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
                <input type="checkbox"
                       data-admin--report-selection-target="all"
                       data-action="change->admin--report-selection#toggleAll"
                       class="size-3.5 accent-accent cursor-pointer">
                {{ 'admin.insight_reports.select_all'|trans }}
            </label>

            <div class="divide-y divide-line">
                {% for item in reports %}
                    {# A <div> and not a <label>, though a label around the whole
                       row would give the checkbox a generous hit target: a
                       label may not contain a <form> or a <details>, and both
                       are here. Browsers happen not to forward label activation
                       from a nested button today, which means the invalid
                       version works — until the row is read by something that
                       is not this browser. The checkbox carries the subject as
                       its accessible name instead.

                       `data-report-row` is what the controller hides when a
                       chip filters this row out. #}
                    <div data-report-row
                         class="flex flex-wrap items-start gap-3 px-4 py-3 hover:bg-hover/50 transition-colors">

                        <input type="checkbox"
                               aria-label="{{ item.subject|default('') ?: 'admin.insight_reports.no_subject'|trans }}"
                               data-key="{{ item.key }}"
                               data-line="{{ item.asLine }}"
                               data-problem="{{ item.problem }}"
                               data-status="{{ item.isPending ? 'pending' : 'handled' }}"
                               data-admin--report-selection-target="row"
                               data-action="change->admin--report-selection#toggleRow"
                               class="size-3.5 mt-1.5 accent-accent cursor-pointer shrink-0">

                        {# The fold is a <details> beside the buttons, not around
                           them: a <form> is flow content and may not live inside
                           a <summary>, and a button that did would toggle the
                           fold on its way to being pressed. #}
                        <details class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-sm group">
                            <summary class="flex items-start gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right mt-1 shrink-0 text-[9px] text-ink-faint w-3
                                          transition-transform group-open:rotate-90" aria-hidden="true"></i>

                                <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1">
                                        <span class="text-xs text-ink-faint font-mono">{{ item.reportedAt|date('Y-m-d H:i') }}</span>

                                        {# WHICH KIND, on every row. The list holds
                                           two things that read almost alike at a
                                           glance — same date, same sender, same
                                           subject — and what an admin does about
                                           one is nothing like what they do about
                                           the other. #}
                                        <span class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide rounded-md px-1.5 py-0.5
                                                     {{ item.kind.value == 'category' ? 'badge-info' : 'badge-neutral' }}">
                                            {{ item.kind.labelKey|trans }}
                                        </span>

                                        {# Handled state on the row rather than
                                           only in a filter: the list is read top
                                           to bottom and "is this one still mine
                                           to do" has to be answerable without
                                           looking anywhere else. #}
                                        {% if item.handledAt is not null %}
                                            <span class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide rounded-md px-1.5 py-0.5 badge-neutral"
                                                  title="{{ 'admin.insight_reports.handled_at'|trans({ '%when%': item.handledAt|date('Y-m-d H:i') }) }}">
                                                {{ 'admin.insight_reports.handled'|trans }}
                                            </span>
                                        {% else %}
                                            <span class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide rounded-md px-1.5 py-0.5 badge-warning">
                                                {{ 'admin.insight_reports.pending_badge'|trans }}
                                            </span>
                                        {% endif %}

                                        {% if item.problem != 'no-insight' %}
                                            <span class="text-[11px] text-ink-muted">{{ report.problem_label(item.problem) }}</span>
                                        {% endif %}

                                        <span class="min-w-0 truncate text-xs text-ink-muted">
                                            {{ 'admin.insight_reports.reported_by'|trans({
                                                '%who%': item.reportedBy ?: 'admin.insight_reports.reporter_gone'|trans,
                                            }) }}
                                        </span>
                                    </div>

                                    <p class="mt-1 truncate text-sm text-ink">
                                        {{ item.subject|default('') ?: 'admin.insight_reports.no_subject'|trans }}
                                    </p>

                                    <p class="mt-0.5 truncate text-xs text-ink-muted">
                                        {% if item.fromName %}{{ item.fromName }} {% endif %}
                                        <span class="font-mono text-ink-faint">{{ item.fromAddress|default('') ?: 'admin.insight_reports.no_sender'|trans }}</span>
                                    </p>

                                    {# The reporter's own words, on the summary and
                                       not inside the fold. InsightReport calls it
                                       the single most valuable column in the
                                       export, and it is the single most valuable
                                       line here for the same reason: it names the
                                       fact a reader would otherwise guess at. #}
                                    {% if item.kind.value == 'insight' and item.source.note %}
                                        <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
                                            <i class="fa-solid fa-quote-left mr-1 text-[9px] text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ item.source.note }}
                                        </p>
                                    {% endif %}
                                </div>
                            </summary>

                            <div class="mt-3 space-y-2 pl-6">
                                {# THE LINE, for both kinds. It is what the copy
                                   button copies and what somebody pastes into a
                                   prompt or an issue, so it is on the page to be
                                   read before it is taken rather than discovered
                                   afterwards in a text file. #}
                                <pre class="text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
                                            rounded-lg bg-zinc-500/10 px-3 py-2">{{ item.asLine }}</pre>

                                {% if item.kind.value == 'insight' %}
                                    {% if item.source.receivedAt is not null %}
                                        <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint">
                                            {{ 'admin.insight_reports.received_at'|trans({ '%when%': item.source.receivedAt|date('Y-m-d H:i') }) }}
                                        </p>
                                    {% endif %}

                                    {# The body, and the only wall of text on the
                                       page — behind the fold, scrolling inside
                                       its own box, so a sixteen-kilobyte
                                       newsletter cannot push the next report off
                                       the screen. #}
                                    {% if item.source.bodyText %}
                                        <pre class="max-h-72 overflow-auto rounded-lg bg-zinc-500/10 px-3 py-2 text-xs text-ink-soft whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">{{ item.source.bodyText }}</pre>
                                    {% else %}
                                        <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint">{{ 'admin.insight_reports.no_body'|trans }}</p>
                                    {% endif %}
                                {% else %}
                                    {# The three answers, side by side and named.
                                       The line above says the same thing in a
                                       form built for pasting; this says it in a
                                       form built for reading, and which one an
                                       admin wants depends on whether they are
                                       about to change a rule or about to send it
                                       to somebody who will. #}
                                    <dl class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-3 gap-y-1 text-xs">
                                        {% for row in [
                                            { key: 'gmail', value: item.source.gmail, signal: null },
                                            { key: 'rules', value: item.source.rules, signal: item.source.rulesSignal },
                                            { key: 'model', value: item.source.model, signal: null },
                                        ] %}
                                            <dt class="text-ink-faint">{{ ('admin.insight_reports.verdict.' ~ row.key)|trans }}</dt>
                                            <dd class="text-ink-soft min-w-0">
                                                {% if row.value %}
                                                    {{ ('tabs.' ~ row.value.value)|trans }}
                                                    {%- if row.signal %} <span class="font-mono text-ink-faint">{{ row.signal }}</span>{% endif %}
                                                {% elseif row.key == 'model' and not item.source.aiAsked %}
                                                    {{ 'admin.insight_reports.verdict.not_asked'|trans }}
                                                {% else %}
                                                    <span class="text-ink-faint">—</span>
                                                {% endif %}
                                            </dd>
                                        {% endfor %}

                                        <dt class="text-ink-faint">{{ 'admin.insight_reports.verdict.headers'|trans }}</dt>
                                        <dd class="text-ink-soft font-mono break-words min-w-0">
                                            {{ item.source.bulkHeaders ?: 'admin.insight_reports.verdict.none'|trans }}
                                            {%- if item.source.listId %} {{ item.source.listId }}{% endif %}
                                        </dd>

                                        <dt class="text-ink-faint">{{ 'admin.insight_reports.verdict.body'|trans }}</dt>
                                        <dd class="text-ink-soft">
                                            {{ ('admin.insight_reports.verdict.body_' ~ (item.source.hasPlainText ? 'text' : 'none'))|trans }}
                                        </dd>
                                    </dl>
                                {% endif %}
                            </div>
                        </details>

                        <div class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1.5">
                            {% if item.handledAt is null %}
                                <form method="post"
                                      action="{{ path('app_admin_insight_reports_handled', { kind: item.kind.value, id: item.id }) }}"
                                      data-turbo-frame="admin-insight-reports">
                                    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('insight_report_handled_' ~ item.kind.value ~ '_' ~ item.id) }}">
                                    <button type="submit"
                                            class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 h-8 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium btn-quiet transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                                        <i class="fa-solid fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                        {{ 'admin.insight_reports.mark_handled'|trans }}
                                    </button>
                                </form>
                            {% endif %}

                            <form method="post"
                                  action="{{ path('app_admin_insight_reports_delete', { kind: item.kind.value, id: item.id }) }}"
                                  data-turbo-frame="admin-insight-reports"
                                  data-turbo-confirm="{{ 'admin.insight_reports.delete_confirm'|trans }}">
                                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('insight_report_delete_' ~ item.kind.value ~ '_' ~ item.id) }}">
                                <button type="submit"
                                        aria-label="{{ 'admin.insight_reports.delete'|trans }}"
                                        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 h-8 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium btn-quiet hover:text-danger hover:bg-danger-soft transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                                    <i class="fa-solid fa-trash" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                </button>
                            </form>
                        </div>

                    </div>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>

            {# ── Export ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
                data-turbo="false", so the browser performs this submission
                itself. Turbo cannot render a download — it would swap the JSON
                into the frame and leave a blank panel. Every other form here
                posts into the frame as usual.

                The ticked keys are written into it by the selection controller,
                and an empty post still means everything — which is what a
                browser with JavaScript off sends, and a download that silently
                returned nothing would be worse than a large file. #}
            <form method="post"
                  action="{{ path('app_admin_insight_reports_export') }}"
                  data-turbo="false"
                  class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3 border-t border-line">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('insight_reports_export') }}">
                <span data-admin--report-selection-target="keys"></span>

                <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                    <p class="text-xs text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">{{ 'admin.insight_reports.export.intro'|trans }}</p>
                    <p class="mt-0.5 text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-relaxed">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation mr-1 text-warning" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        {{ 'admin.insight_reports.export.warning'|trans }}
                        {{ 'admin.insight_reports.export.not_handled'|trans }}
                    </p>
                </div>

                <button type="submit" id="insight-reports-export"
                        class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-2 h-9 px-4 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium
                               text-accent-ink bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-file-arrow-down text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ 'admin.insight_reports.export.submit'|trans }}
                </button>
            </form>
        {% endif %}
    </section>

    {# ── Clearing what is done ───────────────────────────────────────────
       Absent entirely while nothing is handled, rather than present and
       disabled: a delete button that cannot delete anything is furniture, and
       this card is tinted precisely to say "something irreversible lives
       here". The count travels into the lead and the confirm, because a
       confirm that names no number asks the admin to take this panel's word
       for what is about to go — and what goes is the only surviving copy of
       mail somebody took the trouble to report. #}
    {% if handledCount > 0 %}
    {# Not chrome.shell()/chrome.band(): both of those pin `border-line`, and the
       tint is the whole point of this card. Two `border-*` colour utilities on
       one element are resolved by their order in the generated stylesheet, not
       by the order they are written here, so the danger colour cannot simply be
       appended to the macro — the figures are repeated instead, and it is only
       the COLOURS that differ. Same repetition as the reset panel's
       unrecoverable half, which is the other card that has to say this. #}
    <div class="rounded-pane border border-danger/40 bg-pane-soft overflow-hidden">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-danger/40 alert-danger">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-broom text-xs text-danger" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-danger">{{ 'admin.insight_reports.clear_handled.heading'|trans }}</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="{{ chrome.body() }} flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">{{ 'admin.insight_reports.clear_handled.lead'|trans({ '%count%': handledCount }) }}</p>

            <form method="post"
                  action="{{ path('app_admin_insight_reports_clear_handled') }}"
                  data-turbo-frame="admin-insight-reports"
                  data-turbo-confirm="{{ 'admin.insight_reports.clear_handled.confirm'|trans({ '%count%': handledCount }) }}"
                  class="shrink-0">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('insight_reports_clear_handled') }}">
                <button type="submit"
                        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 h-9 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium
                               bg-danger-soft text-danger hover:bg-danger hover:text-white transition-colors cursor-pointer">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-trash" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ 'admin.insight_reports.clear_handled.button'|trans }}
                </button>
            </form>
        </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
</turbo-frame>
